... 174 ### Transactional success for mutations and queries
... 175 
... 176 Use `completeTransactionally: true` with `enqueueMutation` or
... 177 `enqueueMutationBatch` to commit each mutation, its selected success callback,
... 178 and workpool completion bookkeeping together. `enqueueQuery` and
... 179 `enqueueQueryBatch` support the same option:
... 180 
... 181 ```ts
... 182 await pool.enqueueMutation(ctx, internal.tasks.process, args, {
... 183   onComplete: internal.tasks.handleResult,
... 184   onCompleteExcludeKinds: ["canceled"],
... 185   completeTransactionally: true,
... 186 });
... 187 ```
... 188 
... 189 Queries always read an independent snapshot. With this option, the success
... 190 callback and completion bookkeeping commit together, but the query's reads do
... 191 not create dependencies that cause that transaction to retry on concurrent
... 192 writes. The query result may be stale when the callback commits; read any data
... 193 that must still be current within the callback. Without this option, queries run
... 194 through the action batch worker.
... 195 
... 196 Each opted-in query is scheduled in its own mutation wrapper, including queries
... 197 enqueued in a batch. For example:
... 198 
... 199 ```ts
... 200 await pool.enqueueQuery(ctx, internal.tasks.findPending, args, {
... 201   onComplete: internal.tasks.handlePending,
... 202   onCompleteExcludeKinds: ["canceled"],
... 203   completeTransactionally: true,
... 204 });
... 205 ```
... 206 
... 207 For mutations, the callback can read the mutation's writes. For either function
... 208 type, if the success callback or completion bookkeeping throws, the scheduled
... 209 wrapper fails and all its writes roll back. Workpool's periodic recovery then
... 210 marks the work as failed and invokes the callback for `"failed"`, unless
... 211 excluded. Until recovery runs, the job remains running and occupies a
... 212 concurrency slot. There is no separate fallback execution of the success
... 213 callback.
... 214 
... 215 Ordinary work errors still use the existing failure-completion path. Failure and
... 216 cancellation callbacks keep their usual transaction behavior. Excluding every
... 217 kind, or omitting the callback, still allows transactional bookkeeping, without
... 218 a separate completion invocation. Jobs in a batch remain independent
... 219 transactions. Actions do not support this option.
... 220 
... 221 This option requires Convex 1.42 or newer. The work and callback share one
... 222 transaction budget. Workpool uses nested transaction limits to reserve space for
... 223 completion bookkeeping; work that fits by itself may exceed the combined budget.
... 224 Limit overruns or execution failures can still fail the transaction, in which
... 225 case recovery handles it as above.
